{"name":"Lion King","hex":"#dd9933","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A big cat, Panthera leo, native to Africa, India and formerly much of Europe.","A male lion, as opposed to a lioness, which is characterized by having a flowing shaggy mane and taking little part in hunting, which can be done cooperatively."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the light brown color that resembles the fur of a lion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lion"},{"term":"king","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male monarch; a man who heads a monarchy; in an absolute monarchy, the supreme ruler of his nation.","The monarch with the most power and authority in a monarchy, regardless of sex."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crown king, to make (a person) king.","To rule over as king."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Lion King","blocks":[{"text":"The Lion King is a 1994 American animated musical drama film directed by Roger Allers and Rob Minkoff and written by Irene Mecchi, Jonathan Roberts, and Linda Woolverton. Produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation, it features an ensemble voice cast consisting of Matthew Broderick, James Earl Jones, Jeremy Irons, Jonathan Taylor Thomas, Moira Kelly, Niketa Calame, Madge Sinclair, Nathan Lane, Ernie Sabella, Whoopi Goldberg, Cheech Marin, Rowan Atkinson, and Robert Guillaume. The story follows a young lion prince named Simba, who is exiled from his kingdom after his father Mufasa is murdered by his uncle Scar to seize the throne. As he grows up, Simba must decide whether to return home to confront Scar and reclaim his place as king."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3d/The_Lion_King_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lion_King","wikidata":"Q36479"},{"title":"Lion","blocks":[{"text":"The lion is a large cat of the genus Panthera, currently ranging only in Sub-Saharan Africa and India. It has a muscular, broad-chested body; a short, rounded head; round ears; and a dark, hairy tuft at the tip of its tail. It is sexually dimorphic; adult male lions are larger than females and have a prominent mane that extends from the head to the shoulders and chest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion","wikidata":"Q140"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King","wikidata":"Q12097"},{"title":"Lion (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lion is a color that is a representation of the average color of the fur of a lion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion_(color)","wikidata":"Q6555379"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/23/LionKingCharacters.jpg/330px-LionKingCharacters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/23/LionKingCharacters.jpg/330px-LionKingCharacters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A promotional image of the characters from the film. From left to right: Shenzi, Scar, Ed, Banzai, Rafiki, Young Simba, Mufasa, Young Nala, Sarabi, Zazu, Sarafina, Timon, and Pumbaa.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALionKingCharacters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1f/Lionkg2.jpg/250px-Lionkg2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Lionkg2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1f/Lionkg2.jpg/250px-Lionkg2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The alleged \"SEX\" frame","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALionkg2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/15/Earlypresentationreelwhitelionking.jpg/330px-Earlypresentationreelwhitelionking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/15/Earlypresentationreelwhitelionking.jpg/330px-Earlypresentationreelwhitelionking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screenshot from an early presentation reel of The Lion King that shows a white lion cub and a butterfly.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarlypresentationreelwhitelionking.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Okonjima_Lioness.jpg/500px-Okonjima_Lioness.jpg?utm_sou